  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The mandatory risk management standard for any medical device — hardware, SaMD, or AI/ML system — seeking CE marking under EU MDR/IVDR or FDA clearance/approval. Defines the full risk management lifecycle: hazard identification, risk estimation, risk evaluation, risk controls, and post-market monitoring. Non-compliance blocks regulatory approval. Note: this is a paid ISO standard (approx. CHF 148); unlike FHIR or DICOM it is not freely available. Adopt means compliance is mandatory for regulated medical device development — not that the standard document is open access. ISO/TR 24971:2020 provides free implementation guidance excerpts.",
  "mach:editorialReviewedAt": "2026-06-05",
